sys/stack.h -- SPARC V9 stack frame constants, from the platform ABI
====================================================================

The OpenSPARC hypervisor source includes <sys/stack.h> in 13 files but does
not ship it: it belongs to the Solaris kernel build environment. The gnu path
needs it (the sun path takes it from SUNWhea) and it is the only external
header that path reaches. 5 of the 13 files are compiled for ontario/legion;
between them they use four symbols: V9BIAS64, STACK_BIAS, MINFRAME, SA().

These are the 64-bit SPARC V9 stack-frame layout defined by the platform ABI,
which every SPARC V9 System V implementation must use identically. The file is
written from the specification, SPARC Compliance Definition 2.4.1 (SPARC
International, 1999), section 3P-8, Figures 3-16 and 3-17; the header cites
each constant. It replaces a copy of illumos-gate's stack.h (CDDL), so q.bin
has no CDDL component. Checked: q.bin and reset.bin built with either file
are byte-identical.

There is no Linux package to take it from: neither linux-libc-dev nor
libc6-dev for sparc64 defines these constants in a header, and the kernel
hardcodes them in arch/sparc/kernel/*.S, under GPL-2.
